{"id":13,"event":"agent","data":{"type":"text_delta","delta":"**Try “Triage Sprint,” a tiny inbox game.** Each round shows a short incoming message; the player predicts its route, such as **reply, assign, flag, or escalate**. Ollaya makes the same bounded decision, with its confidence and selected action shown beside the result.\n\nClear cases move straight through the fast System 1 loop. Ambiguous or unfamiliar messages visibly trigger System 2 review. It’s quick to understand and makes the key capability easy to see: semantic decisions with confidence, plus escalation when the known policy isn’t enough."},"timestamp":1790819267689}
